{{!
    @template tool_vae/remove_record_page

    The page "Retirer la ligne d'une fiche", below its heading: the refusal and the way back to the list, or the form that
    lists what leaves with the row and asks for a confirmation.

    The template holds no logic: the states exclude one another before (tool_vae\output\remove_record_page). Every value is
    HTML made by the core, placed as it is (triple braces): noticehtml, a notification ($output->notification(), its message
    escaped); continuehtml, the button back to the list ($output->continue_button()); formhtml, the form of the core
    (moodleform::render()), drawn once.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the refusal
    * continuehtml - false, or HTML: the way back to the list
    * formhtml - false, or HTML: the form

    Example context (json):
    {
        "noticehtml": "<div class=\"alert alert-danger\">Moodle still holds the framework of this record.</div>",
        "continuehtml": "<div class=\"continuebutton\"><a href=\"https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/index.php\">Continue</a></div>",
        "formhtml": false
    }
}}
{{#noticehtml}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{/noticehtml}}
{{#continuehtml}}
{{{continuehtml}}}
{{/continuehtml}}
{{#formhtml}}
{{{formhtml}}}
{{/formhtml}}
